                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><div>
<div>Oncology nursing is a course focusing on the prevention, treatment, and care of tumors, comprising 36 credit hours. Clinical experts in the fields of tumor treatment and nursing are invited to deliver lectures. The main content includes: the concept and scope of oncology nursing, tumor prevention and control, ethical and legal issues in oncology nursing, psychological, social, and spiritual issues in oncology nursing, quality of life for cancer patients, major advances and nursing care in tumor treatment, assessment and management of cancer pain, advances in the diagnosis, treatment, and nursing of common cancers, psychological and behavioral interventions for cancer patients, and end-of-life care for cancer patients.</div>
</div></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
